exav-unpack-wasm: third-party notices
=====================================

exav-unpack-wasm and the @exav/unpack-wasm npm package are licensed under the
MIT License (see LICENSE). The package's WebAssembly module is a build of
exav-unpack, its "standard" preset, so it contains the third-party code in
exav-unpack's source and the crates it links. This file gives their notices.
The MIT License and the Apache License 2.0 texts the entries refer to are at
the end of this file; they apply to those components only.


Part 1: code in exav-unpack's source
====================================

libarchive RAR5 reader, BSD-2-Clause (source derivative)
--------------------------------------------------------

exav-unpack's RAR5 decompressor is a Rust port of the decompression core of
libarchive's archive_read_support_format_rar5.c, and the RAR framing of its
PPMd decoder follows libarchive's archive_read_support_format_rar.c and
archive_ppmd7.c, under the same terms.

